1
00:00:05,260 --> 00:00:06,830
Okay, we're headed out-- See you later.

2
00:00:06,830 --> 00:00:07,990
Before you leave,

3
00:00:07,990 --> 00:00:10,560
could you test these noise-cancelling headphones?

4
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:11,820
Yeah, sure. Okay.

5
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:15,710
Go ahead.

6
00:00:15,710 --> 00:00:17,840
Hello, can you hear me?

7
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:23,130
Sheldon, I haven't changed the filter

8
00:00:23,130 --> 00:00:25,780
in the water pitcher in two years.

9
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:31,610
Uh, Bernadette's nickname for you is the virgin pina colada.

10
00:00:35,810 --> 00:00:39,690
Your George Lucas autograph is really a "me" autograph.

11
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:44,100
Yeah, well, once I was too lazy to walk across the hall,

12
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:46,390
so I used your toothbrush.

13
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:50,490
Ooh, and one time when you were asleep,

14
00:00:50,490 --> 00:00:51,920
Amy totally took off her...

15
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:54,350
And that's why you're the best roommate ever.

16
00:00:57,500 --> 00:00:59,670
Now I'm sad I didn't hear it.

17
00:01:00,450 --> 00:01:02,150
So what do you need the headphones for?

18
00:01:02,150 --> 00:01:03,730
Well, I've been struggling for months

19
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:05,500
to come up with a theory of dark matter

20
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:07,230
that doesn't make protons decay.

21
00:01:07,230 --> 00:01:08,780
I'm hoping to finally tackle it

22
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:10,890
by optimizing my work environment.

23
00:01:10,890 --> 00:01:15,620
See, I've got, uh, my tea is at the perfect sipping temperature.

24
00:01:15,630 --> 00:01:18,080
Uh, I have fleece-lined boxer shorts

25
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:19,650
to keep my tushie toasty.

26
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:21,740
And then, oh, last but not least,

27
00:01:21,740 --> 00:01:23,900
this inspirational cat poster,

28
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:26,130
improved with the reassuring face

29
00:01:26,130 --> 00:01:28,470
of physics renegade Richard Feynman.

30
00:01:31,490 --> 00:01:34,340
Is that why you had to take him to Office Depot last night?

31
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:36,440
I don't want to talk about it.

32
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:38,410
There, the place is all yours.

33
00:01:38,410 --> 00:01:39,260
Yeah, have fun.

34
00:01:39,260 --> 00:01:41,190
Oh, I will-- nothing more fun

35
00:01:41,190 --> 00:01:43,550
than a paradigm-shifting evening of science.

36
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:46,650
And you thought it was soaping me up in the shower.

37
00:01:47,810 --> 00:01:48,700
Bye.

38
00:01:49,270 --> 00:01:50,960
Okay.

39
00:01:52,270 --> 00:01:53,980
Here we go.

40
00:01:55,790 --> 00:01:57,220
Proton decay.

41
00:01:58,480 --> 00:01:59,820
Proton decay.

42
00:02:01,250 --> 00:02:02,410
Proton decay.

43
00:02:03,980 --> 00:02:05,200
Proton decay.

44
00:02:07,030 --> 00:02:08,340
Proton decay.

45
00:02:10,110 --> 00:02:11,380
Proton decay.

46
00:02:11,820 --> 00:02:12,830
Hey, we're home.

47
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:17,350
Any progress?

48
00:02:17,350 --> 00:02:18,380
How could there be?!

49
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:20,490
With these constant interruptions.

50
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:26,020
I love him, but if he's broken, let's not get a new one.

51
00:02:55,590 --> 00:02:57,100
What are you doing? It's time to go.

52
00:02:57,180 --> 00:02:59,060
I'm not going to work today.

53
00:02:59,350 --> 00:03:01,140
And would you like to know why?

54
00:03:02,310 --> 00:03:04,060
Ah, you're upset because you spent the whole night working

55
00:03:04,060 --> 00:03:05,850
on dark matter and didn't make a breakthrough,

56
00:03:05,850 --> 00:03:08,030
and now you're worried you made a huge mistake switching fields,

57
00:03:08,030 --> 00:03:09,920
and you're gonna sit around and sulk all day?

58
00:03:10,470 --> 00:03:12,370
Like a big old baby.

59
00:03:14,250 --> 00:03:16,460
Call me if you need anything.

60
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:22,710
I've been cooped up in here too long.

61
00:03:22,770 --> 00:03:24,420
Maybe I need some fresh air.

62
00:03:44,210 --> 00:03:45,090
Penny?

63
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:47,260
Penny?

64
00:03:48,270 --> 00:03:49,130
Penny?

65
00:03:51,670 --> 00:03:52,900
Ugh, what?

66
00:03:52,970 --> 00:03:54,800
You sounded in distress.

67
00:03:54,810 --> 00:03:57,410
I was worried something unpleasant was happening to you.

68
00:03:57,410 --> 00:03:58,780
Like a murder.

69
00:03:58,860 --> 00:04:01,210
Or spontaneous coitus with Leonard.

70
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:06,420
Oh, I'm just doing this awful workout. I hate it.

71
00:04:06,420 --> 00:04:08,940
Well, if you hate it, then why are you doing it?

72
00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:10,240
Although I could ask the same question

73
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:11,770
about coitus with Leonard.

74
00:04:13,510 --> 00:04:15,000
I don't know-- I guess I like that I hate it.

75
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,380
It makes me work harder.

76
00:04:17,430 --> 00:04:20,150
- And to clarify... - The exercise, Sheldon.

77
00:04:21,860 --> 00:04:23,640
Shouldn't you be getting ready for work?

78
00:04:23,750 --> 00:04:25,040
I'm not going.

79
00:04:25,170 --> 00:04:26,720
Would you like to know why?

80
00:04:26,950 --> 00:04:29,550
Uh, you're sad about not getting anything done last night,

81
00:04:29,550 --> 00:04:31,450
so you're gonna sit around and pout about it?

82
00:04:32,420 --> 00:04:35,180
Boy, I'm not nearly as mysterious as I think I am.

83
00:04:37,930 --> 00:04:40,170
- I invented a game. You want to play? - Sure.

84
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:42,370
It's called "Emily or Cinnamon""

85
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:45,930
I give you actual quotes I've heard Raj say,

86
00:04:45,930 --> 00:04:50,350
and you guess if he was talking to his girlfriend or his dog.

87
00:04:54,030 --> 00:04:55,830
Go ahead, make fun.

88
00:04:55,830 --> 00:04:57,010
You can't embarrass me.

89
00:04:57,010 --> 00:04:58,510
I've got a beautiful girlfriend

90
00:04:58,510 --> 00:05:01,190
and a dog who loves me so much she drinks my bathwater.

91
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:06,600
Okay, who was he talking to, Emily or Cinnamon:

92
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:09,840
"I want you to know, the bed feels so lonely

93
00:05:09,850 --> 00:05:11,240
when you're not in it."

94
00:05:17,610 --> 00:05:19,700
I may not be liking this game so much.

95
00:05:21,250 --> 00:05:23,020
Cinnamon. Give me another one.

96
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:25,220
Okay, Emily or Cinnamon:

97
00:05:25,220 --> 00:05:27,690
"Check it out, I got us matching sweaters!"

98
00:05:27,690 --> 00:05:29,700
We all got the Christmas card-- Cinnamon.

99
00:05:31,180 --> 00:05:34,770
You know, a man can care deeply about a woman and a pet.

100
00:05:34,770 --> 00:05:35,950
It's not strange.

101
00:05:35,950 --> 00:05:37,850
Ooh, Emily. I heard him say that to Emily.

102
00:05:39,980 --> 00:05:41,370
Hey, I thought you were staying home.

103
00:05:41,370 --> 00:05:44,210
Yeah, I was, but after talking to Penny,

104
00:05:44,210 --> 00:05:45,650
I realized something.

105
00:05:45,650 --> 00:05:49,480
I... first, she's trying much harder to stay attractive

106
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:51,280
in this relationship than you are.

107
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:56,920
And second...

108
00:05:57,240 --> 00:06:00,060
the reason I may not be progressing in my research is

109
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:03,410
I've created too pleasant of an environment for myself.

110
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:04,900
What do you mean?

111
00:06:04,930 --> 00:06:07,580
According to a classic psychological experiment

112
00:06:07,580 --> 00:06:11,060
by Yerkes and Dodson, in order to maximize performance,

113
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:14,290
one must create a state of productive anxiety.

114
00:06:14,290 --> 00:06:17,770
So I'd like to ask you all to do something for me.

115
00:06:18,110 --> 00:06:19,760
Keep me on my toes.

116
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:21,810
Just throw me off my game.

117
00:06:21,830 --> 00:06:26,210
E-Essentially, go out of your way to make my life miserable.

118
00:06:29,350 --> 00:06:30,160
Hold on.

119
00:06:30,290 --> 00:06:31,870
What's in it for us?

120
00:06:32,210 --> 00:06:34,020
- Well, I suppose... - Okay, we'll do it!

121
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:43,900
Done.

122
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:45,610
33 seconds.

123
00:06:45,610 --> 00:06:48,030
Okay, that'll be our baseline.

124
00:06:48,550 --> 00:06:50,070
You know, I don't want to tell you how to do your job,

125
00:06:50,070 --> 00:06:51,540
but when a mouse completes a maze,

126
00:06:51,540 --> 00:06:53,440
it gets a food pellet.

127
00:06:53,940 --> 00:06:57,220
It also gets its brain plucked out with tweezers.

128
00:06:57,950 --> 00:07:00,200
And his last meal was a food pellet?

129
00:07:00,690 --> 00:07:02,350
You're a monster.

130
00:07:03,990 --> 00:07:05,540
All right, next, we're gonna introduce

131
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:08,570
an anxiety-inducing stimulus, measure your stress levels

132
00:07:08,570 --> 00:07:10,410
and see how it affects your problem-solving rate.

133
00:07:10,410 --> 00:07:11,220
Very well.

134
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:14,600
And good luck-- I'm a pretty laid-back guy.

135
00:07:16,370 --> 00:07:17,550
Ready?

136
00:07:17,550 --> 00:07:18,580
Begin.

137
00:07:41,390 --> 00:07:42,420
Why'd you pop it?

138
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:44,600
I'm sorry, I was aiming for your heart.

139
00:07:48,310 --> 00:07:49,380
Look, I know you don't like it,

140
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:51,200
but that's the point of the experiment.

141
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:52,490
I need to irritate you

142
00:07:52,490 --> 00:07:54,710
to find your optimal anxiety zone.

143
00:07:54,860 --> 00:07:58,810
And you said no to tickling, polka music or watching me eat a banana.

144
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:01,880
Who eats them horizontally?!

145
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:05,980
My mother said that's how good girls do it.

146
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:12,230
Perhaps this was a waste of time.

147
00:08:12,530 --> 00:08:13,500
Sheldon,

148
00:08:13,750 --> 00:08:15,620
you're a remarkable scientist.

149
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:18,310
Just be patient-- I'm sure you'll find the breakthrough

150
00:08:18,310 --> 00:08:19,580
you've been looking for.

151
00:08:19,590 --> 00:08:20,460
Thank you.

152
00:08:20,490 --> 00:08:22,750
And if you only do solid research

153
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:25,360
instead of making a groundbreaking discovery,

154
00:08:25,840 --> 00:08:27,310
what does it matter?

155
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:29,450
"Only do solid research"?!

156
00:08:29,450 --> 00:08:33,330
Uh... I come to you for help, and you insult me?!

157
00:08:33,330 --> 00:08:34,120
I thought the least that you would do would be...

158
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:36,650
Look, your anxiety levels are right in the zone.

159
00:08:37,180 --> 00:08:38,090
Really?

160
00:08:38,090 --> 00:08:39,730
Oh, that's fantastic.

161
00:08:39,730 --> 00:08:41,130
N-Now, wait, they're dropping.

162
00:08:41,130 --> 00:08:42,050
Why are they dropping?

163
00:08:42,050 --> 00:08:43,790
Because you're happy they're elevated.

164
00:08:43,790 --> 00:08:45,770
Oh, that is infuriating!

165
00:08:45,770 --> 00:08:47,330
Ooh, look, they went back up again.

166
00:08:47,330 --> 00:08:48,110
Terrific.

167
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:49,760
Oh, no, they went back down!

168
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:56,200
All right, guys, what game do you want to play?

169
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:57,690
Let's see.

170
00:08:57,690 --> 00:09:00,610
How about "Emily or Cinnamon""

171
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:04,010
You know what? I think it's a little weird

172
00:09:04,010 --> 00:09:05,940
that you remember me saying all these things.

173
00:09:05,940 --> 00:09:09,030
Maybe the truth is-- you're jealous of all my relationships.

174
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:12,390
Oh, maybe I am.

175
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:14,060
Who wouldn't want to be the girl,

176
00:09:14,060 --> 00:09:16,450
or possibly dog, to hear the words:

177
00:09:17,550 --> 00:09:18,750
"You're so lucky.

178
00:09:18,750 --> 00:09:21,070
You have the shiniest hair""

179
00:09:24,940 --> 00:09:26,510
That is a tough one.

180
00:09:26,770 --> 00:09:28,780
Uh, I-I know he brushes both of them.

181
00:09:31,060 --> 00:09:32,360
- Gentlemen... - Yeah.

182
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:36,070
I have figured out the perfect way for you to irritate me.

183
00:09:36,230 --> 00:09:39,790
I'd like you to be my intellectual sparring partners.

184
00:09:39,790 --> 00:09:42,520
From now on, when I make an assertion,

185
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:44,170
I need you to challenge it.

186
00:09:44,420 --> 00:09:47,650
So you just want us to disagree with whatever you say?

187
00:09:47,670 --> 00:09:48,510
Yes.

188
00:09:48,730 --> 00:09:51,400
- And you think that's going to help? - Yes.

189
00:09:52,410 --> 00:09:54,270
Well, I don't think that's gonna help at all.

190
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:55,440
Oh, no, it will.

191
00:09:55,440 --> 00:09:59,160
See, by keeping my mind engaged, I'll become more focused.

192
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:01,040
Howard's right-- that'll never work.

193
00:10:01,740 --> 00:10:04,480
Stop fighting me on the premise. It's scientifically valid.

194
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:06,220
I'm going to advance propositions,

195
00:10:06,220 --> 00:10:07,780
I just want you to challenge me.

196
00:10:07,780 --> 00:10:10,360
I don't think that's what you want at all.

197
00:10:12,410 --> 00:10:13,900
Why, of course it's what I want.

198
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:15,990
Why would I say it's what I want if it's not what I want?

199
00:10:15,990 --> 00:10:18,200
Because it is what you want, and it's not what you said.

200
00:10:20,770 --> 00:10:23,580
I ask you for one simple thing, and you can't even do it.

201
00:10:23,580 --> 00:10:24,420
Yes, we can.

202
00:10:24,420 --> 00:10:26,100
- Yeah, well, then do it. - Nah.

203
00:10:27,710 --> 00:10:29,320
You guys are the worst.

204
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:34,390
Thank you, I think that was helpful.

205
00:10:38,790 --> 00:10:41,250
Whichever rep has the best sales for the quarter

206
00:10:41,250 --> 00:10:43,300
gets a trip for two to Hawaii.

207
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:45,670
That would be so romantic for you and Leonard.

208
00:10:45,670 --> 00:10:47,750
Yeah, clearly you haven't seen him on the beach

209
00:10:47,750 --> 00:10:50,450
walking around with his metal detector.

210
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:52,480
If I were going to Hawaii,

211
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:54,920
I'd spend all my time at the Keck Observatory.

212
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:56,340
Did you know that the telescopes there

213
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:58,190
have better resolution than the Hubble?

214
00:10:58,240 --> 00:10:59,200
Really?

215
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:00,980
Want to go to Hawaii?

216
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:04,580
Ladies?

217
00:11:04,940 --> 00:11:05,970
Ladies...

218
00:11:06,330 --> 00:11:07,220
Ladies?

219
00:11:07,220 --> 00:11:08,200
Come in.

220
00:11:09,550 --> 00:11:10,560
Ladies.

221
00:11:11,050 --> 00:11:11,930
What's up?

222
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:14,890
As you may know, I've been experimenting

223
00:11:14,890 --> 00:11:16,640
with elevated anxiety levels,

224
00:11:16,640 --> 00:11:17,670
and I thought,

225
00:11:17,670 --> 00:11:19,960
what better way to increase my discomfort

226
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:21,610
than to subject myself to an evening

227
00:11:21,610 --> 00:11:24,300
of tasteless uncensored crotch talk?

228
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:29,870
What exactly do you think goes on here?

229
00:11:30,450 --> 00:11:31,160
Well...

230
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:33,000
conversations that you wouldn't be comfortable having

231
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,730
in front of the opposite sex.

232
00:11:34,730 --> 00:11:37,880
You know, who has the best cervix.

233
00:11:37,880 --> 00:11:40,320
Which sanitary napkin is all the rage right now.

234
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:44,320
Men's buttocks, and how you want to pat and squeeze them.

235
00:11:46,770 --> 00:11:48,400
We were talking about Penny's job.

236
00:11:49,150 --> 00:11:50,410
And how difficult it is to do

237
00:11:50,410 --> 00:11:52,150
when she's bloated, cranky and crampy?

238
00:11:52,150 --> 00:11:53,000
Continue.

239
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:58,060
Sheldon, we are just people.

240
00:11:58,060 --> 00:12:00,470
We talk about the same things you guys talk about.

241
00:12:00,570 --> 00:12:02,710
You talk about if werewolves can swim?

242
00:12:03,890 --> 00:12:05,440
See, Leonard says yes,

243
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:07,480
but I say it depends on if the human could swim

244
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:09,340
before he was bitten. What do you think?

245
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,850
Let's just talk about our periods.

246
00:12:14,890 --> 00:12:15,910
No, hold on.

247
00:12:16,030 --> 00:12:18,900
All canines instinctively know how to swim.

248
00:12:18,900 --> 00:12:21,640
Why wouldn't a werewolf have the same abilities?

249
00:12:21,920 --> 00:12:24,260
Well, they're not a hundred percent wolf.

250
00:12:24,260 --> 00:12:27,040
They're a werewolf-- that's only part wolf.

251
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:28,880
It's like comparing apples to oranges.

252
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:30,170
Thank you.

253
00:12:30,690 --> 00:12:33,350
Oh, and technically, it's apples that turn into were-oranges

254
00:12:33,350 --> 00:12:34,520
when the moon is full.

255
00:12:36,490 --> 00:12:37,750
Hey, this is fun.

256
00:12:38,370 --> 00:12:40,450
We should do it sometime when you aren't all PMS'ing.

257
00:12:40,450 --> 00:12:41,150
Bye.

258
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:52,460
What is going on?

259
00:12:53,410 --> 00:12:56,090
Uh, I need to keep my anxiety at the right level,

260
00:12:56,090 --> 00:12:59,980
so I'm using Darth Vader, the Joker, and Godzilla's roar

261
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:01,660
to keep me in that sweet spot.

262
00:13:03,030 --> 00:13:05,930
Uh, I tried including Taylor Swift in the mix,

263
00:13:05,930 --> 00:13:08,100
but turns out I love her.

264
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:13,350
Well, at least listen to it through headphones.

265
00:13:13,350 --> 00:13:15,270
I'm trying to sleep. Good night.

266
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:17,560
Boy!

267
00:13:19,290 --> 00:13:22,590
Taylor was right-- haters gonna hate, hate, hate, hate, hate.

268
00:13:25,750 --> 00:13:27,770
You've been working so much lately,

269
00:13:28,110 --> 00:13:30,090
I'm glad you didn't forget about date night.

270
00:13:30,090 --> 00:13:31,590
Of course.

271
00:13:33,770 --> 00:13:34,680
Sheldon.

272
00:13:34,870 --> 00:13:35,760
Yeah.

273
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:39,680
Maybe you want to put the notebook away and talk to me.

274
00:13:39,750 --> 00:13:41,330
I can do both.

275
00:13:41,330 --> 00:13:44,180
No, my brain is working at optimal capacity.

276
00:13:44,180 --> 00:13:46,220
No, I can have a conversation with you

277
00:13:46,220 --> 00:13:49,670
and solve the dark matter proton decay problem at the same time.

278
00:13:51,310 --> 00:13:52,720
Fine. How was your day?

279
00:13:52,720 --> 00:13:54,200
Oh, you said it.

280
00:13:56,870 --> 00:13:57,760
Sheldon.

281
00:13:58,120 --> 00:13:59,890
Sheldon, I'm worried about you.

282
00:14:00,310 --> 00:14:01,270
You're not eating,

283
00:14:01,270 --> 00:14:03,340
you haven't slept in days,

284
00:14:03,340 --> 00:14:06,250
and, to be honest, that cap is starting to smell.

285
00:14:07,440 --> 00:14:08,450
I know.

286
00:14:08,620 --> 00:14:10,600
It's replaced Godzilla

287
00:14:10,610 --> 00:14:11,980
as my principle source of anxiety.

288
00:14:17,140 --> 00:14:19,440
Okay, so it's one vote Emily, one vote Cinnamon.

289
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:21,680
Penny, you're the tiebreaker.

290
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:25,830
Say the quote again.

291
00:14:26,890 --> 00:14:30,530
"It's just so perfect that we're both Libras."

292
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:36,920
Wow, this is hard.

293
00:14:37,730 --> 00:14:38,590
I'm gonna say Cinnamon.

294
00:14:38,590 --> 00:14:39,350
- Yes! - Yes!

295
00:14:39,350 --> 00:14:40,610
Come on!

296
00:14:42,450 --> 00:14:44,120
That was the last one, I promise.

297
00:14:44,130 --> 00:14:45,050
We won't play anymore.

298
00:14:45,050 --> 00:14:46,160
Thank you.

299
00:14:46,390 --> 00:14:48,830
'Cause if she ever found out, it would hurt her feelings.

300
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:50,800
Emily's feelings?

301
00:14:52,360 --> 00:14:53,580
Yes, Emily.

302
00:14:53,580 --> 00:14:55,330
- Nice! Yay! - Good job!

303
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:59,200
Whatever. Where's Sheldon?

304
00:14:59,260 --> 00:15:00,170
Date night.

305
00:15:00,170 --> 00:15:01,990
Mmm, that can't be much fun for Amy.

306
00:15:01,990 --> 00:15:04,370
You know, at work today, he tried his first Red Bull.

307
00:15:04,380 --> 00:15:05,280
What happened?

308
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:08,750
He chased a squirrel around the quad for a while and...

309
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:11,560
...then threw up in my car.

310
00:15:13,810 --> 00:15:15,960
Don't you think you should make him stop all this?

311
00:15:16,130 --> 00:15:18,440
I don't know-- he's not really hurting anybody.

312
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:21,550
You didn't have to scoop vomit out of your glove compartment.

313
00:15:22,690 --> 00:15:24,190
He is getting a lot of work done.

314
00:15:24,190 --> 00:15:26,910
He had a pretty interesting take on proton decay.

315
00:15:26,910 --> 00:15:30,510
Wow, if he cracks that, it's a game changer, guys.

316
00:15:30,650 --> 00:15:32,550
It'll completely redefine our understanding

317
00:15:32,550 --> 00:15:34,260
of the physical universe.

318
00:15:36,010 --> 00:15:37,590
Hmm, it would.

319
00:15:38,150 --> 00:15:40,220
Okay, back to "Emily or Cinnamon""

320
00:15:42,790 --> 00:15:46,960
"How can such a little girl eat such a big steak""

321
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:52,180
Sheldon,

322
00:15:52,430 --> 00:15:54,430
I want you to take that cap off.

323
00:15:54,940 --> 00:15:58,250
That nagging tone is helping my anxiety, yeah.

324
00:15:58,250 --> 00:16:00,620
But if you could maybe just go ten percent less shrill,

325
00:16:00,620 --> 00:16:03,010
that'd really put the zip-a-dee in my doo-dah.

326
00:16:03,790 --> 00:16:05,760
I'm sorry, but you know we agreed

327
00:16:05,760 --> 00:16:07,790
not to bring work to date night.

328
00:16:07,790 --> 00:16:09,520
There you go, perfect.

329
00:16:10,420 --> 00:16:12,080
Sheldon, stop it, I'm not kidding.

330
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:14,850
Take the cap off, and put the notebook away.

331
00:16:14,870 --> 00:16:18,080
But after months of struggling, I'm finally making progress.

332
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:21,300
You don't need to drive yourself crazy in order to be productive.

333
00:16:21,300 --> 00:16:23,250
Or do I, hmm?

334
00:16:23,270 --> 00:16:25,450
Sir Isaac Newton wrote his Principia

335
00:16:25,450 --> 00:16:27,320
while convinced he was an armadillo.

336
00:16:28,560 --> 00:16:29,660
That's not true.

337
00:16:29,660 --> 00:16:31,390
Yeah, well, maybe it is, maybe it isn't.

338
00:16:31,390 --> 00:16:33,280
I have been hallucinating lately.

339
00:16:35,310 --> 00:16:37,090
Sheldon, this has to stop.

340
00:16:37,090 --> 00:16:39,720
You need to get some sleep and take care of yourself.

341
00:16:39,720 --> 00:16:42,810
Amy, I have gotten more done in the last few days

342
00:16:42,810 --> 00:16:44,870
than I have since I made the switch to dark matter.

343
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:47,720
What if I stop doing this, and it all goes away?

344
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:51,730
Your thoughts and ideas come from you, not from your anxiety.

345
00:16:51,730 --> 00:16:53,130
Hmm, perhaps.

346
00:16:53,130 --> 00:16:54,800
But I'm not taking the cap off.

347
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:57,690
It's one thing to make yourself miserable,

348
00:16:57,690 --> 00:17:00,320
but you're making everyone around you miserable, too.

349
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:04,120
Now, I'm telling you for the last time-- take the cap off.

350
00:17:05,430 --> 00:17:06,340
Really?

351
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:08,790
What if I don't?

352
00:17:08,840 --> 00:17:12,210
And before you answer that, can I have my dessert?

353
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:15,610
And then she threw me out.

354
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:20,590
Me, her very own boyfriend.

355
00:17:20,750 --> 00:17:23,340
When all I've done is try to help humanity reach

356
00:17:23,340 --> 00:17:26,080
a more profound understanding of the world we live in.

357
00:17:29,950 --> 00:17:31,150
Yeah, well, women--

358
00:17:31,150 --> 00:17:32,320
what are you gonna do?

359
00:17:35,260 --> 00:17:38,160
I knew you'd understand, Armadillo Isaac Newton.

360
00:17:43,130 --> 00:17:45,130
Okay...

361
00:17:45,310 --> 00:17:47,080
Here we are.

362
00:17:49,260 --> 00:17:51,600
What are you trying to pull?

363
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:54,310
The president of science isn't in here.

364
00:17:55,630 --> 00:17:57,730
You lie down, he'll be here in a minute.

365
00:17:58,930 --> 00:17:59,950
Okay.

366
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:02,960
Hey, I thought you were trying to trick me.

367
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:07,720
Now, you just get comfortable.

368
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:10,000
No, no, comfort is the enemy.

369
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:11,390
You know what's comfortable?

370
00:18:11,390 --> 00:18:15,400
Slippers and blankets and panda bears.

371
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:20,620
Imagine a panda bear with Richard Feynman's face on it.

372
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:24,580
Warm up the car, Leonard, it's poster time.

373
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:26,750
Maybe in the morning.

374
00:18:26,750 --> 00:18:28,030
Yeah, you get some sleep.

375
00:18:28,030 --> 00:18:30,640
No, I don't want to go to sleep-- you can't make me.

376
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:31,780
You're right, we can't.

377
00:18:31,780 --> 00:18:33,280
Yeah, darn straight, you can't.

378
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:34,870
Try to tell a grown man to go to sleep...

379
00:18:34,870 --> 00:18:37,790
* Soft kitty *

380
00:18:37,790 --> 00:18:40,000
* Warm kitty *

381
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:41,990
* Little ball of fur... *

382
00:18:41,990 --> 00:18:43,650
That's not gonna work.

383
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:48,410
* Happy kitty, sleepy kitty *

384
00:18:48,410 --> 00:18:49,180
* Purr *

385
00:18:49,190 --> 00:18:51,740
* Purr, purr *

386
00:18:54,850 --> 00:18:56,530
You know, he can be a lot of trouble,

387
00:18:56,530 --> 00:18:59,990
but when I see him lying here asleep like this,

388
00:19:00,450 --> 00:19:02,020
I just think...

389
00:19:03,070 --> 00:19:06,270
how easy it would be to hold a pillow over his face.

390
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:14,080
Wow, you look like you got some rest.

391
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:15,740
Oh, I'm feeling much better.

392
00:19:15,740 --> 00:19:18,040
And I've also been continuing to make progress

393
00:19:18,040 --> 00:19:20,660
without artificially raising my anxiety levels.

394
00:19:20,670 --> 00:19:23,160
I turned on the heat in my car and some vomit came out,

395
00:19:23,170 --> 00:19:25,340
so my levels-- right up there.

396
00:19:26,220 --> 00:19:27,020
Hey, guys.

397
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:28,470
Mind if Emily joins us for lunch?

398
00:19:28,470 --> 00:19:29,870
- Yeah, sure. - Yeah, no problem. Of course not.

399
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:33,070
So I hear you guys have been playing a little game.

400
00:19:33,190 --> 00:19:35,670
Well, um, we were just kidding around.

401
00:19:35,670 --> 00:19:38,460
Well, you may think it's funny that Raj is sweet and sensitive,

402
00:19:38,460 --> 00:19:40,250
but I think it's sexy.

403
00:19:44,090 --> 00:19:47,390
Ugh, why is there dog hair in your mouth?

